-- title:
--   Splitting a p-divisible group by complementary idempotents
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a field, $p$ a prime, $h$ a natural number, and let $H$ be a $p$-divisible group of height $h$ over $F$ in the sense of the project structure: a family of commutative rings $H.\mathrm{level}\,v$ ($v \in \mathbb{N}$), each a cocommutative Hopf $F$-algebra that is finite and free as an $F$-module of rank $p^{vh}$, together with surjective bialgebra maps $H.\mathrm{transition}\,v : H.\mathrm{level}\,(v+1) \to H.\mathrm{level}\,v$ whose kernels are the ideals generated by the image of the augmentation ideal under the $p^v$-fold sum map $\mathtt{nsmulAlgHom}$. Assume given two families $\varepsilon, \varepsilon'$ of bialgebra endomorphisms of the $H.\mathrm{level}\,v$ such that each $\varepsilon v$ and each $\varepsilon' v$ is idempotent under composition, the two composites $\varepsilon v \circ \varepsilon' v$ and $\varepsilon' v \circ \varepsilon v$ both equal the trivial endomorphism $\iota \circ \epsilon$ (counit followed by the structure map $F \to H.\mathrm{level}\,v$), the convolution product of $\varepsilon v$ and $\varepsilon' v$ in the convolution monoid `WithConv` is the identity, and both families commute with the transition maps, i.e. $H.\mathrm{transition}\,v \circ \varepsilon (v+1) = \varepsilon v \circ H.\mathrm{transition}\,v$ and likewise for $\varepsilon'$. The conclusion asserts the existence of natural numbers $h_1 + h_2 = h$, of $p$-divisible groups $H_1$ of height $h_1$ and $H_2$ of height $h_2$ over $F$, and of families of bialgebra maps $\pi_1 v : H.\mathrm{level}\,v \to H_1.\mathrm{level}\,v$ and $j_2 v : H_2.\mathrm{level}\,v \to H.\mathrm{level}\,v$, such that: each $\pi_1 v$ is surjective and $\pi_1 v \circ H.\mathrm{transition}\,v = H_1.\mathrm{transition}\,v \circ \pi_1 (v+1)$; each $j_2 v$ is injective and $H.\mathrm{transition}\,v \circ j_2 (v+1) = j_2 v \circ H_2.\mathrm{transition}\,v$; the kernel of $\pi_1 v$ is the ideal of $H.\mathrm{level}\,v$ generated by the image under $j_2 v$ of the augmentation ideal (the kernel of the counit) of $H_2.\mathrm{level}\,v$; an element $b$ of $H.\mathrm{level}\,v$ satisfies $\varepsilon' v\,b = b$ if and only if it lies in the image of $j_2 v$; and there is a family of $F$-algebra maps $\sigma_1 v : H_1.\mathrm{level}\,v \to H.\mathrm{level}\,v$ with $\pi_1 v \circ \sigma_1 v = \mathrm{id}$ and $\sigma_1 v \circ \pi_1 v = \varepsilon v$.
--
--   This is the exactness form of the splitting of a $p$-divisible group over a field by a pair of complementary Hopf-algebra idempotents: on the level of group schemes it produces a short exact sequence $0 \to H_2 \to H \to H_1 \to 0$, with $H_2$ cut out as the $\varepsilon'$-fixed part and with an algebra (not bialgebra) section of the quotient map realising $\varepsilon$. It refines the companion statement [`PDivisibleGroup.exists_pDivisibleGroup_surjective_bijective_tensorProduct_of_comp_eq_self_of_field`](thm.html#PDivisibleGroup.exists_pDivisibleGroup_surjective_bijective_tensorProduct_of_comp_eq_self_of_field), which it cites, and is used in the sub/quotient step of the two-step tower construction for modular curves, [`ModularCurve.exists_twoStepTower_raynaudQuotient_descent_finPts_jHNeronObjectAtP_of_finPtsWitness_of_bridgePins`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_twoStepTower_raynaudQuotient_descent_finPts_jHNeronObjectAtP_of_finPtsWitness_of_bridgePins).
